      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '1: A plate used by different Eskani families. Some Eskani families would
    pass down plates made by their ancestors to their kids as a generational keepsake.



    2:
    A plate used by Cleoni families. The plates were used for decorations within
    Celoni homes and businesses to honor their culture and give thanks to the makers
    of the dish.



    3: An urn used by Thebrean families. It is common in Thebrean
    families to cremate a loved one who has passed and put their ashes in a decorative
    urn to show respect to their relatives.

'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
